  "scope": "# Review: 61c0bcd32328\n\nTask/source: `61c0bcd32328`, selected generator `2.1.0`, SHA-256 `4f45d334880485ba8e7926f352f6f9c919dad53df3a9b868af43703964dff4ec`.\nDefect \u2192 repair: singleton corner components were legal but unreachable because general scenes sampled `_SHAPES[1:]`; the sampler now uses all `_SHAPES`.\nCanonical rule: unchanged; clockwise exact source SHA-256 `0dc3328fe8ad885a19f7c620a4d641ffc733e8cc641a331d01b3e88410c5f64e`.\nPrototype: added an unselected episode-level `clockwise|counterclockwise` direction variant with the canonical source as the default.\nFocused task tests: **18 passed**, including the singleton regression, fixed-setting episodes, four queries, canonical hashes, public masking, and portable runtime evidence paths.\nExact Racket: **14/14 prototype labels** and **8/8 canonical occurrences** matched; both direction programs refute the opposite setting on every retained demonstration.\nRepair witness: exact Racket copies a sampled one-cell TL component to TR; the historical ignore-singleton rival is refuted at cell `(0,9)`.\nAdversarial authored scope: **192 episodes**, three count schedules, 12/12 corner-profile/band singleton witnesses, and public/numeric boundaries passed.\nSupplementary tickets: the schedule-receipt request is already represented in current tooling; peer `033db13a9d37` has one Racket-confirmed column-major shortcut witness requiring maintainer assessment.\nRemaining main-task failures: none in the scoped checks. Limits are finite seeds/settings and no production approval or training admission for the prototype.",
